i) Valuation Currency(ies) and Measurement
The valuation shall ordinarily be expressed in Indian Rupees (INR). Where, owing to the nature
of the assets, business operations, transactions, or market practices, any value is expressed in a
currency other than INR, the Registered Valuer shall provide reasons for the use of such
currency. In such cases, the valuation report shall also disclose the applicable exchange rate
used for conversion into INR, the date as of which such exchange rate has been considered,
and the source from which the exchange rate has been obtained.
